# Fixed 2026-10-03, defect 169, lane depth (panel 184's R5 and R6).
# Symptom: brackets a reader sees nested stopped the compiler at exit 134
# from a few hundred deep on the 8 MB stack a POSIX shell gives a process:
# `g(g(...))` at 200 (`build` from 100), `[[...]]` and `f"{f"{...}"}"` at
# 250, `((...))` at 600 (panel 184's shared table).
# Cause: the parser and every pass after it recurse once per bracket, and
# the stack was the shell's. Every command now runs on a thread whose stack
# the compiler chooses (`selfhost/main.hero`).
# This case: a call and an `f` hole each nested 2,000 deep, panel 184's
# floor as measured under that thread
# (`docs/records/log/2026-10-03-1130-panel-184-r5-landed-every-command-runs-on-a-thread-whose-stack-the-compiler-chooses.md`),
# built and run. Parentheses are measured there and not held here: the
# formatter drops a pair that groups nothing, so `((1))` has no canonical
# spelling deeper than `1`.

function g(v: i64) -> i64
    return v

function calls() -> i64
    return g(
